<title>USA: US West says court denies appeal.</title>
<headline>US West says court denies appeal.</headline>
<dateline>ENGLEWOOD, Colo. 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>US West Communications Group said on Monday that the King County Superior Court in Washington State ruled on the company's appeal and upheld a ruling issued earlier this year by the Washington Utilities and Transportation Commission denying U S West a rate hike.</p>
<p>The company said the court instead ruled to decrease rates in net by $91.5 million, and ordered U S West to set a flat fee of $10.50 a month for basic local service.</p>
<p>The company said it is &quot;disappointed&quot; with the ruling, and will continue to exercise its legal and procedural options as appropriate</p>
</text>
